# device-layer-0004.
# Location: where the device is, once, through the platform's own location service: CoreLocation on macOS and
# iOS, LocationManager on Android (the platform's, no Play Services), navigator.geolocation in a browser.
#
#   current-position   `<latitude> <longitude> <accuracy>`, degrees to six places and metres, or not-determined
#                      (ask first: request-permission location), denied, unavailable, or failed
#
# A host with no such capability (the server, the memory host) answers `unavailable`. Every answer is text from the
# closed set above, so an app compares strings and no platform enum ever reaches it.

load ./native/{platform}/location
  find read-position
  find follow-position

task current-position
  like text
  send back
    call read-position

# the answer above now and at every change the platform reports, to `handler`, until the task it answers is called.
# Any number at once, each dropped by its own task, and one subscription to the platform between them, ended by
# the last drop. A watcher started while others run hears the current answer at once
task watch-position
  take handler
    like task
      take value, like text
  like task
  send back
    call follow-position
      read handler
